//
// Probe: math.interpolation (Bund/src/stdlib/functions/math/interp.rs:12-38).
//
// X is the top list and Y the next, then xp, which must be a FLOAT (:29).
// Lists go through conv(FLOAT) element by element (statistics/get_data.rs:149).
//
"probe: halfway between the second and third points" println
2.5 [ 10.0 20.0 30.0 ] [ 1.0 2.0 3.0 ] math.interpolation println

"probe: integer lists convert to float" println
1.5 [ 10 20 30 ] [ 1 2 3 ] math.interpolation println

"probe: below the first point" println
0.0 [ 10.0 20.0 30.0 ] [ 1.0 2.0 3.0 ] math.interpolation println

"probe: beyond the last point" println
5.0 [ 10.0 20.0 30.0 ] [ 1.0 2.0 3.0 ] math.interpolation println
